  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 207 AM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nAfter another chilly night and morning Sunday, temperatures will \nrebound back into the 60s/70s Sunday afternoon with plenty of \nsunshine. A large upper trough is expected to develop to our west \nnext week, but move very slowly east. This will place our region in \nsouthwesterly flow aloft for several days. Temperatures will climb \nback above normal as Gulf moisture slides back into our region. Rain \nchances stay near zero until midweek when mid level lift increases, \nespecially over the far west.",
